<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>

<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

<title>Digital Learning Hub</title>

<style>

*{
    margin:0;
    padding:0;
    box-sizing:border-box;
    font-family:Arial, sans-serif;
}

body{
    background:#f1f5f9;
    color:#1e293b;
}

/* HEADER */

header{
    background:#0f172a;
    color:white;
    padding:35px 20px;
    text-align:center;
    border-bottom:5px solid #14b8a6;
}

header h1{
    font-size:38px;
    margin-bottom:8px;
}

header p{
    color:#cbd5e1;
}

/* MAIN CONTAINER */

.wrapper{
    width:90%;
    max-width:1100px;
    margin:30px auto;
}

/* CONTENT CARDS */

.box{
    background:white;
    padding:28px;
    margin-bottom:25px;
    border-radius:12px;
    border:1px solid #dbe3ec;
    box-shadow:0 5px 15px rgba(15,23,42,0.08);
}

.box h2{
    color:#0f766e;
    margin-bottom:20px;
    border-bottom:2px solid #ccfbf1;
    padding-bottom:10px;
}

/* FORM */

.study-form{
    background:#f8fafc;
    padding:20px;
    border-radius:8px;
}

label{
    display:block;
    margin-top:12px;
    font-weight:bold;
}

input,
select,
textarea{
    width:100%;
    padding:12px;
    margin-top:6px;
    margin-bottom:12px;
    border:1px solid #cbd5e1;
    border-radius:6px;
    font-size:15px;
}

input:focus,
select:focus,
textarea:focus{
    outline:none;
    border-color:#14b8a6;
}

button{
    background:#0f766e;
    color:white;
    border:0;
    padding:12px 25px;
    border-radius:6px;
    cursor:pointer;
    font-size:16px;
}

button:hover{
    background:#115e59;
}

/* QUESTIONS */

details{
    margin:15px 0;
    border:1px solid #dbe3ec;
    border-radius:8px;
    background:#f8fafc;
    padding:15px;
}

summary{
    cursor:pointer;
    font-weight:bold;
    color:#0f172a;
    font-size:17px;
}

.question-content{
    margin-top:18px;
    padding:15px;
    background:white;
    border-radius:7px;
}

pre{
    background:#17202a;
    color:#d1fae5;
    padding:15px;
    margin:12px 0;
    border-radius:6px;
    overflow-x:auto;
}

.answer{
    color:#047857;
    font-weight:bold;
    margin:12px 0;
}

.explanation{
    line-height:1.7;
}

ul{
    margin-left:25px;
    line-height:1.8;
}

/* FOOTER */

footer{
    text-align:center;
    background:#0f172a;
    color:#cbd5e1;
    padding:20px;
    margin-top:40px;
}

/* MOBILE */

@media(max-width:600px){

    header h1{
        font-size:30px;
    }

    .wrapper{
        width:94%;
    }

    .box{
        padding:20px;
    }

}

</style>

</head>

<body>


<header>

<h1>📚 Digital Learning Hub</h1>

<p>
HTML, HTTP, XML and Web Communication - Case Study
</p>

</header>


<div class="wrapper">


<!-- REGISTRATION -->

<div class="box">

<h2>Course Registration</h2>

<form
class="study-form"
onsubmit="event.preventDefault(); alert('Course registration completed successfully!');"
>

<label>Student Name</label>

<input
type="text"
name="student"
placeholder="Enter your full name"
required
>


<label>Email Address</label>

<input
type="email"
name="email"
placeholder="Enter your email"
required
>


<label>Select Course</label>

<select name="course">

<option>Web Development</option>
<option>Database Management</option>
<option>Java Programming</option>
<option>Cloud Computing</option>

</select>


<label>Additional Message</label>

<textarea
rows="4"
name="message"
placeholder="Enter your comments">
</textarea>


<button type="submit">
Enroll Now
</button>

</form>

</div>


<!-- QUESTIONS -->

<div class="box">

<h2>Case Study - Questions and Solutions</h2>


<!-- QUESTION 1 -->

<details>

<summary>Question 1 - Embedding a Video</summary>

<div class="question-content">

<h3>Options</h3>

<pre>
A. &lt;movie&gt;
B. &lt;video&gt;
C. &lt;media&gt;
D. &lt;film&gt;
</pre>

<p class="answer">
Correct Answer: B. &lt;video&gt;
</p>

<p class="explanation">

HTML5 provides the <b>&lt;video&gt;</b> element for displaying
video content directly on a webpage. It can provide controls
such as play, pause, volume and fullscreen.

In an online learning platform, this element can be used
to display recorded lectures and educational videos.

</p>

</div>

</details>


<!-- QUESTION 2 -->

<details>

<summary>Question 2 - Choosing a Form Method</summary>

<div class="question-content">

<h3>Options</h3>

<pre>
A. GET
B. DELETE
C. POST
D. PATCH
</pre>

<p class="answer">
Correct Answer: C. POST
</p>

<p class="explanation">

The POST method sends form information through the HTTP
request body rather than placing the submitted values in
the URL.

For student registration, POST is preferable because
personal information should not normally be exposed through
the URL.

For actual security, the connection should also use HTTPS.

</p>

</div>

</details>


<!-- QUESTION 3 -->

<details>

<summary>Question 3 - Semantic Navigation Element</summary>

<div class="question-content">

<h3>Options</h3>

<pre>
A. &lt;article&gt;
B. &lt;main&gt;
C. &lt;nav&gt;
D. &lt;footer&gt;
</pre>

<p class="answer">
Correct Answer: C. &lt;nav&gt;
</p>

<p class="explanation">

The <b>&lt;nav&gt;</b> element is specifically designed
to represent a collection of important navigation links.

For example, an educational website may contain links
for Home, Courses, Results, Assignments and Contact.

Using the semantic navigation element makes the structure
of the webpage clearer to browsers and assistive technologies.

</p>

</div>

</details>


<!-- QUESTION 4 -->

<details>

<summary>Question 4 - Identifying Valid XML</summary>

<div class="question-content">

<h3>Options</h3>

<pre>
A. &lt;student&gt;&lt;name&gt;Alex&lt;/name&gt;

B. &lt;student&gt;&lt;name&gt;Alex&lt;/name&gt;&lt;/student&gt;

C. &lt;student&gt;&lt;name&gt;Alex&lt;/student&gt;&lt;/name&gt;

D. &lt;student&gt;&lt;name&gt;Alex&lt;/name
</pre>

<p class="answer">
Correct Answer: B
</p>

<h3>Reason</h3>

<ul>

<li>
A → The root element is not closed.
</li>

<li>
B → Both elements are properly opened and closed.
</li>

<li>
C → The closing tags are incorrectly nested.
</li>

<li>
D → The closing bracket is missing.
</li>

</ul>

<p class="explanation">

XML follows strict syntax rules. Every opening tag must
have a matching closing tag, and elements must be correctly
nested inside one another.

</p>

</div>

</details>


<!-- QUESTION 5 -->

<details>

<summary>Question 5 - Browser and Server Protocol</summary>

<div class="question-content">

<h3>Options</h3>

<pre>
A. SMTP
B. FTP
C. HTTP
D. DHCP
</pre>

<p class="answer">
Correct Answer: C. HTTP
</p>

<p class="explanation">

HTTP stands for HyperText Transfer Protocol. It is commonly
used for communication between a web browser and a web server.

When a student accesses an online course, the browser sends
HTTP requests to the server. The server then responds with
resources such as HTML documents, CSS files, JavaScript and
other web content.

SMTP is mainly used for email communication, FTP is used
for file transfer, and DHCP is used for network configuration.

</p>

</div>

</details>


</div>

</div>


<footer>

<p>
© 2026 Digital Learning Hub
</p>

<p>
Internet Programming Case Study
</p>

</footer>


</body>

</html>
